        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: സാമ്രാജ്യം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സാമ്രാജ്യം — sāmrājyaṁ — \"an empire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ സാമ്രാജ്യം ഒരുപാട് രാജ്യങ്ങളിൽ പരന്നു കിടന്നു. ā sāmrājyaṁ orupāṭŭ rājyaṅṅaḷil parannu kiṭannu. That empire stretched over many countries."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One ruler over many kingdoms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സാമ്രാജ്യം (sāmrājyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit sāmrājya, \"complete or universal sovereignty, empire\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
